<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>Use your notes in AI apps - Terp Notes</title>
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="/favicon.png" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles/main.css" />
    <style>
        .wrap { max-width: 820px; margin: 2rem auto; padding: 0 1rem; }
        .card { background: #fff; border: 1px solid #E5E7EB; border-radius: 12px; padding: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }
        .muted { color: #6B7280; font-size: 0.92rem; }
        code, pre { background: #F3F4F6; border-radius: 6px; padding: 2px 6px; word-break: break-all; }
        pre { padding: 0.75rem; white-space: pre-wrap; }
        .row { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; gap: 0.75rem; padding: 0.5rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #F3F4F6; flex-wrap: wrap; }
        .row:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
        form { display: flex; gap: 0.5rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
        form input { flex: 1; min-width: 200px; padding: 0.55rem 0.75rem; border: 1px solid #D1D5DB; border-radius: 8px; }
        #new-token { display: none; background: #F0FDF4; border: 1px solid #BBF7D0; }
        h2 { margin-top: 0; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <%- include('partials/topnav', { active: '' }) %>
    <main class="wrap">
        <h1>Use your notes in ChatGPT and Claude</h1>
        <p class="muted">Terp Notes has an MCP server, so AI apps can search course notes and read them while you study. It can only read notes you can already see; it can't upload, change or delete anything.</p>

        <section class="card">
            <h2>1. Create an access token</h2>
            <form id="create-form">
                <input name="name" aria-label="Token name" placeholder="Name, e.g. ChatGPT on my laptop" maxlength="60" />
                <button type="submit" class="button primary">Create token</button>
            </form>
            <div id="new-token" class="card" style="margin-top: 1rem;" role="status">
                <p style="margin-top: 0;"><strong>Copy this now.</strong> You won't see it again.</p>
                <p>Token: <code id="token-value"></code></p>
                <p>Private connector URL (for ChatGPT and Claude.ai): <code id="token-url"></code></p>
                <p class="muted" style="margin-bottom: 0;">Treat both like a password. If one leaks, revoke it below.</p>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="card">
            <h2>2. Connect your AI app</h2>
            <p><strong>ChatGPT:</strong> Plugins → <em>+</em> → Add custom MCP server. Paste your private connector URL and choose <em>No authentication</em> (the token is in the URL).</p>
            <p><strong>Claude.ai:</strong> Settings → Connectors → Add custom connector, and paste your private connector URL.</p>
            <p><strong>Claude Code:</strong></p>
            <pre>claude mcp add --transport http terp-notes <%= baseUrl %>/mcp --header "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN"</pre>
            <p><strong>Other MCP clients:</strong> server URL <code><%= baseUrl %>/mcp</code>, header <code>Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN</code>.</p>
            <p class="muted">Tools: <code>list_courses</code>, <code>search_notes</code>, <code>get_note</code>, and <code>search</code> / <code>fetch</code> for ChatGPT.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="card">
            <h2>Your tokens</h2>
            <% if (tokens.length === 0) { %>
                <p class="muted" id="no-tokens">No active tokens.</p>
            <% } %>
            <div id="token-list">
                <% tokens.forEach(t => { %>
                    <div class="row token-row" data-id="<%= t.id %>">
                        <span><strong><%= t.name %></strong> <span class="muted"><code><%= t.prefix %>…</code> · created <%= new Date(t.createdAt).toLocaleDateString() %> · <%= t.lastUsedAt ? 'last used ' + new Date(t.lastUsedAt).toLocaleString() : 'never used' %></span></span>
                        <button class="button danger" onclick="revoke('<%= t.id %>')">Revoke</button>
                    </div>
                <% }) %>
            </div>
        </section>
    </main>
    <%- include('partials/footer') %>
    <script>
        const baseUrl = <%- JSON.stringify(baseUrl) %>;
        document.getElementById('create-form').addEventListener('submit', async (e) => {
            e.preventDefault();
            const res = await fetch('/api/ai-access/tokens', {
                method: 'POST',
                headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
                body: JSON.stringify({ name: e.target.name.value })
            });
            const data = await res.json();
            if (!res.ok) return alert(data.error || 'Could not create a token');
            document.getElementById('token-value').textContent = data.token;
            document.getElementById('token-url').textContent = `${baseUrl}/mcp/${data.token}`;
            document.getElementById('new-token').style.display = 'block';
            e.target.reset();
        });
        async function revoke(id) {
            if (!confirm('Revoke this token? Apps using it will stop working.')) return;
            const res = await fetch(`/api/ai-access/tokens/${id}/revoke`, { method: 'POST' });
            if (res.ok) document.querySelector(`.token-row[data-id="${id}"]`)?.remove();
        }
    </script>
</body>
</html>
